      "title": "House Republicans urge DoJ to further investigate ‘key witnesses’ in Epstein case",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/10/house-republicans-epstein-investigation",
      "description": "<p>Republicans on House panel criticize US government’s investigation into Jeffrey Epstein and Ghislaine Maxwell</p><p>Republicans on the House oversight committee released a report on Tuesday criticizing the federal government’s handling of the investigations into Jeffrey Epstein and his associate, Ghislaine Maxwell, and called on the Department of Justice to interview “key witnesses, investigate Epstein associates accused of criminal activity, and ensure survivors have access to their records”.</p><p>“The federal government has failed the survivors of Jeffrey Epstein and Ghislaine Maxwell’s horrific crimes for decades,” James Comer, the Republican congressman who chairs the committee, said in a <a href=\"https://oversight.house.gov/release/house-oversight-committee-releases-report-on-the-federal-governments-mishandling-of-epstein-and-maxwell-criminal-investigations/\">statement</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/10/house-republicans-epstein-investigation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-10T18:44:17"
    },
